.TH SWAPOFF 2 "August 2026"
.SH NAME
swapoff \- remove a block device from paging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B int swapoff(const char *special);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Swapoff
stops allocation from the named block device and makes every anonymous page
which still uses that device resident before closing it.  Other swap devices
remain available throughout the operation.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero is returned on success.  On failure, \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
[EPERM]
The caller is not the super-user.
.TP 15
[EINVAL]
The named device is not active swap.
.TP 15
[ENOMEM]
There is insufficient physical memory to make the remaining pages resident.
.TP 15
[EIO]
An error occurred while paging data in from the device.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swapon (2),
.BR swapoff (8)
